    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for LawDog hinges on a favorable matchup against Ryne Nelson, who anchors three of our strongest plays. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** leads the team with an elite 80.31 score, bolstered by a prime #2 spot and a soft matchup against Montero. Right behind him, **Jung Hoo Lee** (64.82) and **Luis Arraez** (63.57) provide a high-floor, high-average core. **Jung Hoo Lee** benefits significantly from a +10% order bonus as our lead-off spark, while **Luis Arraez** capitalizes on a strong RHP platoon edge to maintain our 5x5 average standing. **Will Smith** remains a foundational start at C1 (63.24) despite the pending lineup, as his xwOBA profile remains too robust to bench against a hittable Canning.\n\nWe are hunting upside in the outfield with **Daulton Varsho** (61.57), who earns a boost from projected wind-out conditions and a favorable platoon matchup against Warren. Conversely, **Gavin Sheets** (42.96) and **Jonathan Aranda** (45.30) are walking a tightrope today; both are penalized heavily by the sub-3.20 xERA marks of their respective opponents, Bradish and Sheehan. **Taylor Ward** was the most difficult exclusion from the starting nine, landing just below our 40.0 floor at 39.23. While his leadoff spot provided a +10% lift, a difficult matchup against Jax and a -19% SP skill penalty pushed the optimizer to prioritize the more efficient platoon advantages offered by **Matt Chapman** (59.49) and **Geraldo Perdomo** (57.99).\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of \"Lineup Pending\" designations for **Will Smith**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Luis Arraez**, **Drew Gilbert**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Matt Chapman**. If any of these names shift down the order upon final posting, their efficiency scores will slide, particularly for **Drew Gilbert** (49.56), who is already anchored by an unfavorable #8 spot. We continue to monitor the status of **Cal Raleigh** and **Yainer Diaz**, as both remain sidelined on the IL, leaving our catching depth thin. We are positioned to chase stolen bases and volume today, but we must be prepared to swap **Gavin Sheets** for the bench if his order position slips below #4.",
